From befedab4d367fc7e7e1a8c3067cb90da853dc6ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:05:52 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] [guilib] Allow textures to be mipmapped

Large textures are drawn with plain bilinear filtering. When a photo is
drawn at close to its own size while a zoom animation changes the scale,
the pixel grids beat against each other: fine light and dark detail
shows a grid of sharp and blurred patches that sweeps across the image,
e.g. during a Ken Burns zoom in a picture add-on.

Add an opt-in mipmap="true" texture attribute. Images loaded through the
large texture manager then get mipmaps, so a texture decoded larger than
the control and drawn smaller is filtered smoothly. Kodi's own slideshow
already does this when high quality downscaling is on. The flag is part
of the large texture key, so a mipmapped and a plain copy of the same
image don't share one texture. Textures without the attribute load as
before.

Assisted-By: Claude
